             the web, where the caller passes t(...). The card's OWN strings (empty dash, trend a11y) live in the
             P1/S10 table "HighlightCard".
  a11y     : icon is decorative → .accessibilityHidden(true); the card is one combined VoiceOver element
             (.accessibilityElement(children: .combine)); the trend chip announces "Increased/Decreased by {value}"
             instead of the arrow glyph; Dynamic Type via system fonts; reduce-motion safe (glow is a static shadow).
  telemetry: view.opened surface="HighlightCard" via HighlightCardSurface.reportOpen (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.

